{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:local-isometry","title":"def:local-isometry","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":121,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:local-isometry","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:isometry]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:local-isometry","line":227,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Local Isometry]\n\\label{def:local-isometry}\n\n\\uses{def:isometry, def:metric-preserving, def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nA map between Riemannian manifolds is a local isometry if every point has a neighborhood on which it is an isometry onto an open subset. Equivalently, it is a local diffeomorphism preserving the metric pointwise.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Local Isometry] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6c6f63616c2d69736f6d65747279\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aisometry\">↗ def:isometry</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ametric-preserving\">↗ def:metric-preserving</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <p></p>A map between Riemannian manifolds is a local isometry if every point has a neighborhood on which it is an isometry onto an open subset. Equivalently, it is a local diffeomorphism preserving the metric pointwise. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:isometry-symm","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-equidim-local-diffeomorphism","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:isometry","title":"def:isometry","label":"def:isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","label":"def:metric-preserving"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:characterize-local-isometry","title":"prop:characterize-local-isometry","label":"prop:characterize-local-isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","title":"lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry","label":"lem:riemannian-covering-local-isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#exer:characterize-local-isometry","title":"exer:characterize-local-isometry","label":"exer:characterize-local-isometry"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:local-isometry","title":"def:local-isometry","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Local Isometry]\n\\label{def:local-isometry}\n\n\\uses{def:isometry, def:metric-preserving, def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nA map between Riemannian manifolds is a local isometry if every point has a neighborhood on which it is an isometry onto an open subset. Equivalently, it is a local diffeomorphism preserving the metric pointwise.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blu